script = ExtResource("1_6cn5t")
entry_name = "Joining Text"
description = "Python joins strings with the + operator. Put the exact spaces you want inside the strings.

first = \"Juan\"
last = \"Dela Cruz\"
full = first + \" \" + last
print(full)

The output is:

Juan Dela Cruz

Convert between text and numbers with str() and int():

year = int(\"21\") * 2
print(year)          # 42
print(str(7) + \"!\")  # 7!

The game's Python runtime supports these basic string and number conversions. It does not expose console input(), so lessons and programs should declare their values in code."
keyword = "join"
language = "python"
category = "Easy"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://c8mblthys4abt"
